// Sign in with Google on iOS. Both values are public identifiers, not
// secrets, and stay empty until the iOS OAuth client exists in Google Cloud.
// While they are empty the app does not offer Google on iOS; the app also
// needs the same client id as its GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID build define.
//
// GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID       the iOS client id, such as
//                            1234567890-abcdef.apps.googleusercontent.com
// GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID  the same id reversed, such as
//                            com.googleusercontent.apps.1234567890-abcdef
//                            (the URL scheme Google returns to the app on)
GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID =
GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID =
